Spec: SpecDD Path PSI Reference

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Represent clickable IntelliJ references for SpecDD path and glob candidates.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDPathReference.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDPathReference.kt

Can read:
  ./SpecDDPathResolver.kt
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/references/SpecDDPathReferenceBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Resolve exact path candidates to one PSI target when possible.
  Resolve glob candidates to all matching PSI targets.
  Return no target when a candidate is unresolved or ignored.
  Expose candidate text as canonical reference text.
  Keep references soft so unresolved paths are handled by the path warning annotator.
  Support target rename for exact path candidates by replacing only the final path segment.
  Support target move/rebind for exact path candidates by recomputing the path from the original prefix style.
  Preserve `/` project-root paths as project-root-relative paths during rebind.
  Preserve `./` and `../` spec-relative paths as spec-relative paths during rebind.
  Use document-backed text replacement when applying rename or rebind changes.
  Leave glob candidates unchanged during rename and rebind.

Must not:
  Report diagnostics.
  Modify target files.
